    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/17-rainbow-fishes-and-co/chilatherina-sentanensis/",
      "html": "<p>The specific name was chosen after Lake Sentani, elevation 75 m above sea level, where the type specimens were collected. Later expeditions to the lake showed that the species can be found rather in the affluents of the lake than in the lake itself.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/17-rainbow-fishes-and-co/chilatherina-sentanensis/",
      "html": "<p>The introduction to the hobby came much later and to this day this attractive fish is seen only sporadically in the trade. As with most rainbowfish, one has to be a bit patient until the animals show their full splendid coloration, but from that moment on the patience is more than rewarded.</p>"
    }
  ],
